---
import { url } from '../lib/urls';
---
<main class="written-story">
    <section class="story-hero story-hero--detail">
      <div class="container">
        <a href={url("/stories/index.html")} class="story-back"><span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">arrow_back</span> All Patient Stories</a>
        <span class="story-hero-kicker">Breast cancer</span><h1 class="story-hero-title">Facing cancer while growing a family</h1>
        <p class="story-hero-byline">Amy Jensen · Originally published <time datetime="2019-07-01">July 1, 2019</time></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="story-detail-media" aria-label="Amy's photograph"><div class="container">
      <figure class="story-detail-frame"><img src={url("/images/story-amy-jensen.jpg")} alt="Amy Jensen with her husband Chad and their son Jacob"></figure>
    </div></section>
    <article class="story-article" aria-label="Amy's story"><div class="container"><div class="story-article-body">
      <p>Amy Jensen was hoping for another baby when persistent changes in her breast led her to seek further testing. On the morning of a planned biopsy, she learned she was pregnant. She later pursued the biopsy at around thirteen weeks of pregnancy and was diagnosed with HER2-positive invasive ductal carcinoma.</p>
      <p>Amy and her husband, Chad, shared the news with their daughters. Alongside concerns about treatment, Amy worried about how losing her hair might affect her children.</p>
      <p>At eighteen weeks pregnant, Amy underwent surgery with Dr. Teresa Reading at IMC Hospital, including a mastectomy and reconstruction. Her subsequent care at Utah Cancer Specialists included chemotherapy and Herceptin.</p>
      <p>Chad researched scalp cooling and connected with Dr. Gregory Litton. Amy used the <a href={url('/dignicap/')}>DigniCap system</a> during treatment. Although initially anxious about discomfort, she found it more tolerable than expected, and Dr. Litton observed that she was retaining her hair.</p>
      <p>The July 2019 account reported that Amy was cancer-free. Her family had also welcomed Jacob, born in December 2018.</p>
      <div class="story-source"><p>Adapted from the original Utah Cancer Specialists article. Photo from Utah Cancer Specialists.</p><p>This account reflects the original publication date. Each patient’s experience is different; individual results do not predict another person’s outcome.</p></div>
      <a class="story-link" href={url("/stories/dukhi-hong.html")}>Read Dukhi’s story <span class="material-symbols-rounded" aria-hidden="true">arrow_forward</span></a>
    </div></div></article>
  </main>
  <!-- Story CTA -->
  <section class="story-cta">
    <div class="container story-cta-inner">
      <h2 class="story-cta-heading">Every story starts with a first appointment.</h2>
      <div class="story-cta-actions">
        <a href={url("/contact.html")} class="btn btn--white"><span class="material-symbols-rounded">phone</span> Contact Us</a>
        <a href={url("/stories/index.html")} class="story-cta-link">More patient stories <span class="material-symbols-rounded">arrow_forward</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
